From 69c8395aac66af0acf75c9a1db620b917890a161 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: J P <jpwatters@mac.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 40/41] Ethernet through the M5Stack W5500 PoE base, alongside
 Wi-Fi

net/eth_w5500.c looks for a W5500 on the Tab5's M5-Bus at boot (MOSI G18,
MISO G19, SCK G5, CS G52, INT G51, RST G48; SPI3, because SPI2 is the SD
card's). No base: one log line, nothing else changes. Base fitted: an
Ethernet netif comes up next to the Wi-Fi station with a higher route
priority (200 vs 100), so while it has a DHCP address it carries new
traffic - the NAS relay, the web page, spots, SNTP, updates - and when the
cable is pulled traffic falls back to Wi-Fi by itself. qmx.local is
announced on both (mDNS predefined ETH_DEF interface).

- wifi.c: the got-IP services (mDNS, SNTP, web server, rigctld) are now
  wifi_net_services_start(), called from both links; the default event loop
  may already exist (Ethernet starts in parallel).
- net_is_up() (Ethernet OR Wi-Fi) replaces wifi_is_connected() wherever the
  question is "can I reach the network": radio_relay (connect, discovery),
  spots, rbn, dxcluster, psk_rx, pskreporter, pskr_self, wspr_self,
  band_conditions, update_check, ota_update, time_sync's SNTP checks.
- Bottom bar and web page show "Ethernet" and its address while it is the
  link in use; /api/status has an "eth" object; the diag log a line.
- PHY reset pin set to G48 explicitly: IDF's default is GPIO 5, our SCK.
- sdkconfig / sdkconfig.defaults: CONFIG_ETH_SPI_ETHERNET_W5500=y.

Full idf.py build (ESP-IDF v5.4.4, standing patches applied) succeeds;
check_tx_guard, check_unattended_tx, check_dirty_bits, check_web,
check_webui and check_docs clean. Not yet run with a base on a Tab5.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
